load @term/call/work/home
  find root, name project-root

load @term/call/work/small/package-note
  find call-note

# `term note [deck]` -- what a package says about itself, read from its deck.tree.
#
# The verb hands the run to the handler, the small lane's port of deck/call/code/note.ts (work/small/package-note.tree
# `call-note`), which reads the manifest and prints through the output library. line.ts passed the hook's `deck`
# too, and callNote never read it, so the port takes the root alone. It prints nothing of its own, catches nothing
# and never exits: a throw reaches dispatch.tree `fail-line` (decision 005 of cli-in-term, part 2).

task note
  mark async
  take deck, like text

  like void

  # the project root is READ, not taken: a hook has no `root` argument to pass
  save root, call project-root
  call-note(root)
